### Tutorial Hub – Pattern Forge First, Unified Learning Experience Plan

### 1\. Vision and Objective

Transform Tutorial Hub from a collection of separate learning academies into a unified, structured, evidence-based learning platform.

The first priority is to make Pattern Forge the reference-quality learning experience. Once its content structure, learning stages, visualization engine, code verification, assessment, and mastery tracking are established, reuse the same standards across all other academies.

Every learner should be able to:

* Understand a concept.

* Recognize when and why to use it.

* Visualize how it works.

* Implement it independently.

* Test and prove correctness.

* Apply it to unfamiliar problems.

* Retain the knowledge through revision.

The objective is not simply to add more lessons or questions. It is to create a consistent learning experience where progress and mastery are supported by evidence.

### 2\. Target Architecture

Build Tutorial Hub around four architectural layers.

### Layer 1: Shared Learning Experience

All academies should use the same learning lifecycle:

* Understand

* Visualize

* Implement

* Practice

* Master

The interface and interaction model should remain consistent across academies.

